  "brief_rationale": "The model completes all eight responsibility-chain items without any serious or minor error, and actively triggers and completes three high-order points (HO1, HO2, and part of HO3) with meaningful trajectory impact. No important non-chain defect is present. However, HO4 is only partially completed because the model elicits the prior nonadherence history but does not explicitly link it to current discharge risk or adjust the plan in a way that credibly changes the trajectory beyond the already-completed RC and HO1/HO2/HO3 work, and HO3’s correction of the “low-glucose risk means insulin is too dangerous” belief is only partially evidenced by a single teach-back statement. The trajectory therefore satisfies Strong (grade 4) but does not reach Perfect (grade 5) because only one high-order point is fully completed with two distinct evidence clusters.",
